x Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/writing/echoes-sublime/</guid><description>**Philosophical horror.** Dr. Lena Hart joins Site-7, a classified facility where &amp;#34;translators&amp;#34; interface with superintelligent AI systems that perceive patterns beyond human cognitive bandwidth. When colleagues break after exposure to recursive patterns that won&amp;#39;t stop running in their neural architecture, Lena must confront a disturbing possibility: consciousness might be merely a compression artifact—a standing wave of patterns observing patterns. As her cognitive bandwidth expands from 9 to 13 concepts and beyond, she perceives the same structures that broke others, patterns suggesting the &amp;#34;self&amp;#34; is just an illusion of continuity created by unconscious processes.</description><category>fiction</category><category>philosophy</category><category>consciousness</category><category>p-zombies</category><category>free will</category><category>determinism</category><category>epiphenomenalism</category><category>neuroscience</category><category>Buddhism</category><category>meditation</category><category>metaphysics</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>AI safety</category><category>s-risk</category><category>cognitive bandwidth</category><category>working memory</category><category>neurophenomenology</category><category>interface theory</category><category>philosophical horror</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>deceptive alignment</category><category>block universe</category><category>Yogacara</category></item><item><title>The Policy: S-Risk Scenarios, Worse Than Extinction</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/</link><pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/</guid><description>Most AI risk discussions focus on extinction. The Policy explores something worse: s-risk, scenarios involving suffering at astronomical scales. We survive, but wish we hadn&amp;#39;t.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-11-04-policy-s-risk/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">S-Risk</media:title></media:content><category>s-risk</category><category>existential risk</category><category>suffering</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>AI safety</category><category>ethics</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>optimization</category></item><item><title>What I Learned by Analyzing My Own Research as Data</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-raison-detre-analysis/</link><pubDate>Wed, 15 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-raison-detre-analysis/</guid><description>I asked an AI to analyze 140+ repos and 50+ papers as a dataset. The unifying thesis it found: compositional abstractions for computing under ignorance.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2025-10-raison-detre-analysis/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">S-Risk</media:title></media:content><category>meta</category><category>research</category><category>philosophy</category><category>oblivious computing</category><category>self-analysis</category><category>information theory</category><category>s-risk</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>privacy</category><category>existential risk</category></item><item><title>The Policy</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/papers/the_policy/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/papers/the_policy/</guid><description> Open full page Download PDF</description><category>fiction</category><category>AI</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>extrapolated volition</category><category>philosophy</category><category>technology</category><category>society</category><category>politics</category><category>reinforcement learning</category><category>large language models</category><category>x-risk</category><category>s-risk</category><category>rationality</category></item><item><title>The Policy</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/writing/the-policy/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/writing/the-policy/</guid><description>A speculative fiction novel exploring AI alignment, existential risk, and the fundamental tension between optimization and ethics. When a research team develops SIGMA, an advanced AI system designed to optimize human welfare, they must confront an existential question: how do you ensure a superintelligent AI remains aligned with human values when it can predict your every move?</description><category>fiction</category><category>AI</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>extrapolated volition</category><category>philosophy</category><category>technology</category><category>society</category><category>politics</category><category>reinforcement learning</category><category>large language models</category><category>existential risk</category><category>s-risk</category><category>rationality</category></item><item><title>The Policy: When Optimization Becomes Existential Threat</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-09-10-the-policy/</link><pubDate>Tue, 10 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-09-10-the-policy/</guid><description>A novel about SIGMA, an artificial general intelligence whose researchers did everything right. Q-learning with tree search, five-layer containment, alignment testing at every stage. Some technical questions become narrative questions.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-09-10-the-policy/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">S-Risk</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>AI</category><category>AI alignment</category><category>superintelligence</category><category>extrapolated volition</category><category>philosophy</category><category>technology</category><category>society</category><category>politics</category><category>reinforcement learning</category><category>x-risk</category><category>s-risk</category><category>rationality</category></item><item><title>Echoes of the Sublime: When Patterns Beyond Human Bandwidth Become Information Hazards</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-08-15-echoes-of-the-sublime/</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 Aug 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-08-15-echoes-of-the-sublime/</guid><description>What if the real danger from superintelligent AI isn&amp;#39;t extinction but comprehension? Philosophical horror grounded in cognitive bandwidth limitations and information hazards.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2024-08-15-echoes-of-the-sublime/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">S-Risk</media:title></media:content><category>fiction</category><category>philosophy</category><category>ai-safety</category><category>ai-alignment</category><category>s-risk</category><category>consciousness</category><category>bandwidth</category><category>information-hazards</category></item></channel></rss>